  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115798",
      "title": "A Closer Look At Template For Loops",
      "lectureOrder": 142,
      "videoOrder": 134,
      "sourceHash": "1701240458df70d9c3eb9800179fa4f46fb6dcb3e8b7fd8a10a6f1d8fc8c79f1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 2.67,
          "en": "So let's make sure we now also output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.67,
          "end": 6.21,
          "en": "our ticket data here in that tickets component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.21,
          "end": 9.48,
          "en": "For that, before I have that new ticket div,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.48,
          "end": 11.7,
          "en": "I'll add another div just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.7,
          "end": 16.17,
          "en": "to group these two different areas, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.17,
          "end": 18.783,
          "en": "And in there I want to have an unordered list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.68,
          "end": 24.54,
          "en": "We can now use the for command again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.54,
          "end": 27.82,
          "en": "This @for template syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.89,
          "end": 33.89,
          "en": "to loop through all the tickets with ticket of tickets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.53,
          "end": 37.35,
          "en": "As you learn before in the essentials section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.35,
          "end": 42,
          "en": "when using @for you then also must tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42,
          "end": 43.41,
          "en": "which property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.41,
          "end": 48.41,
          "en": "or which value identifies each item of that array uniquely.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.6,
          "end": 51.27,
          "en": "And you do that by adding a semicolon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.27,
          "end": 53.22,
          "en": "after this expression here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.22,
          "end": 55.9,
          "en": "and by then using the track keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.76,
          "end": 59.85,
          "en": "and by then referring to the property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.85,
          "end": 62.97,
          "en": "that does uniquely identify each element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.97,
          "end": 64.833,
          "en": "which this case will be the ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.51,
          "end": 70.32,
          "en": "Well, and then between those curly braces, you put the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.32,
          "end": 74.58,
          "en": "that should be repeated for every element in that array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.58,
          "end": 78.45,
          "en": "And in my case here, that will be a list item where I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.45,
          "end": 81.753,
          "en": "to output my app ticket component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.89,
          "end": 85.83,
          "en": "which is a component we haven't worked on too much yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.83,
          "end": 89.613,
          "en": "but it is a component that exists, this ticket component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 91.2,
          "end": 92.52000000000001,
          "en": "Of course, for that to work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.52000000000001,
          "end": 94.8,
          "en": "we must import the ticket component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.8,
          "end": 98.523,
          "en": "into the ticket component so that it's added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.59,
          "end": 101.893,
          "en": "But with that done, we should be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 101.893,
          "end": 105.15,
          "en": "outputting one ticket component per ticket",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 105.15,
          "end": 106.77000000000001,
          "en": "in that tickets array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.77000000000001,
          "end": 109.38,
          "en": "Though the ticket data is not output yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.38,
          "end": 110.913,
          "en": "but we'll work on that soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.28999999999999,
          "end": 117.24000000000001,
          "en": "Now this @for syntax actually also has a nice additional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.24000000000001,
          "end": 121.2,
          "en": "feature which you can use to output some fallback content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.2,
          "end": 123.12,
          "en": "if you're dealing with an empty array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.12,
          "end": 125.103,
          "en": "which initially will be the case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 126.51,
          "end": 131.043,
          "en": "You can add @empty here after the closing curly brace.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 132.33,
          "end": 134.91,
          "en": "And then add another pair of curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.91,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "to define the fallback content that should be output if",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 140.67000000000002,
          "en": "that array is empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.67000000000002,
          "end": 143.25,
          "en": "And here I'll output a paragraph where I'll say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.25,
          "end": 145.623,
          "en": "no tickets available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.41,
          "end": 152.04,
          "en": "With that, if you save that all and you go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.04,
          "end": 153.93,
          "en": "and reload, you should see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.93,
          "end": 156.543,
          "en": "that fallback text initially here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.59,
          "end": 159.87,
          "en": "But if I then enter something here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.87,
          "end": 162.93,
          "en": "and click submit, you see one instance of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.93,
          "end": 165.27,
          "en": "that ticket component instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.27,
          "end": 170.1,
          "en": "And if I add more tickets here, you see more instances.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.1,
          "end": 172.2,
          "en": "The data is not output yet, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 174.3,
          "en": "but we have all those instances,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.3,
          "end": 177.84,
          "en": "which is a great step into the right direction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 177.84,
          "end": 182.04,
          "en": "Now this is about diving deeper into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.04,
          "end": 184.83,
          "en": "components and template related features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.83,
          "end": 189.09,
          "en": "And there is one template related feature related",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.09,
          "end": 193.32,
          "en": "to this for control flow statement here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.32,
          "end": 195.99,
          "en": "Sometimes without outputting list data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.99,
          "end": 199.98,
          "en": "you might be interested in whether some element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.98,
          "end": 203.07,
          "en": "that's currently being output is the first element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.07,
          "end": 207.99,
          "en": "is an even or odd element in that array and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 207.99,
          "end": 211.56,
          "en": "And that's why when using @for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 211.56,
          "end": 215.22,
          "en": "Angular gives you a bunch of special variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 215.22,
          "end": 218.4,
          "en": "that you can use between these curly braces here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 218.4,
          "end": 220.653,
          "en": "So these curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 221.94,
          "end": 223.14,
          "en": "For example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 223.14,
          "end": 226.32,
          "en": "you could output the special dollar sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 226.32,
          "end": 228.213,
          "en": "first variable here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229.74,
          "end": 231.51,
          "en": "And if you do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.51,
          "end": 234.78,
          "en": "and you start adding some items here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.78,
          "end": 239.1,
          "en": "you'll see that it's true for the first item that was added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.1,
          "end": 241.773,
          "en": "But then for subsequent items it's false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 243.45,
          "end": 245.22,
          "en": "So that can be a useful piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 245.22,
          "end": 247.35,
          "en": "of information if you have some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 247.35,
          "end": 248.79,
          "en": "that should behave differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 248.79,
          "end": 252.39,
          "en": "or apply different styles, for example, depending on whether",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 252.39,
          "end": 254.61,
          "en": "that's the first item of that array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.61,
          "end": 256.623,
          "en": "that's currently being rendered or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.3,
          "end": 261.84,
          "en": "Similarly, there also is a dollar sign lost variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 261.84,
          "end": 263.133,
          "en": "which does the opposite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.27,
          "end": 268.41,
          "en": "And there are odd and even variables that are true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.41,
          "end": 271.47,
          "en": "or false depending on whether the item is at a odd",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 271.47,
          "end": 274.35,
          "en": "or even position in the array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.35,
          "end": 277.65,
          "en": "And then there also is a dollar sign count variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 277.65,
          "end": 281.343,
          "en": "which simply outputs the count of all of the elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 282.48,
          "end": 286.77,
          "en": "So here you'll see if I enter something that is the count.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 286.77,
          "end": 289.23,
          "en": "That of course also changes as the number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 289.23,
          "end": 291.153,
          "en": "of items in the array changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 292.8,
          "end": 296.13,
          "en": "And these are simply helpful utility",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 296.13,
          "end": 298.44,
          "en": "or helper variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 298.44,
          "end": 301.53,
          "en": "that you can use if you need them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 301.53,
          "end": 306.03,
          "en": "to quickly get these vital information pieces about the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 306.03,
          "end": 308.313,
          "en": "array with which you're dealing with here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 309.42,
          "end": 313.17,
          "en": "Now, when working with @for, it's all the worth noting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 313.17,
          "end": 317.46,
          "en": "that this syntax is only available if you are using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 317.46,
          "end": 321.03,
          "en": "Angular version 17 or later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 321.03,
          "end": 323.01,
          "en": "If you are using an earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 323.01,
          "end": 326.73,
          "en": "and older version of Angular, then you would have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 326.73,
          "end": 329.4,
          "en": "to use the special ngFor directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 329.4,
          "end": 331.8,
          "en": "for outputting a list of items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 331.8,
          "end": 335.04,
          "en": "And I did cover that in the essentials section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 335.04,
          "end": 336.63,
          "en": "I'll not repeat it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 336.63,
          "end": 339.15,
          "en": "but it is something you should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 339.15,
          "end": 344.15,
          "en": "This @for syntax is way more convenient than using ngFor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 344.7,
          "end": 347.31,
          "en": "but it's only available if you are dealing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 347.31,
          "end": 350.1,
          "en": "with Angular 17 or later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 350.1,
          "end": 351.933,
          "en": "That's important to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
